{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1073","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Vasya and Robot"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya has got a robot which is situated on an infinite Cartesian plane, initially in the cell $$$(0, 0)$$$. Robot can perform the following four kinds of operations: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — move from $$$(x, y)$$$ to $$$(x, y + 1)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — move from $$$(x, y)$$$ to $$$(x, y - 1)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — move from $$$(x, y)$$$ to $$$(x - 1, y)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — move from $$$(x, y)$$$ to $$$(x + 1, y)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya also has got a sequence of $$$n$$$ operations. Vasya wants to modify this sequence so after performing it the robot will end up in $$$(x, y)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya wants to change the sequence so the length of changed subsegment is minimum possible. This length can be calculated as follows: $$$maxID - minID + 1$$$, where $$$maxID$$$ is the maximum index of a changed operation, and $$$minID$$$ is the minimum index of a changed operation. For example, if Vasya changes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RRRRRRR"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RLRRLRL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the operations with indices $$$2$$$, $$$5$$$ and $$$7$$$ are changed, so the length of changed subsegment is $$$7 - 2 + 1 = 6$$$. Another example: if Vasya changes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"DDDD"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"DDRD"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the length of changed subsegment is $$$1$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are no changes, then the length of changed subsegment is $$$0$$$. Changing an operation means replacing it with some operation (possibly the same); Vasya can't insert new operations into the sequence or remove them."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Vasya! Tell him the minimum length of subsegment that he needs to change so that the robot will go from $$$(0, 0)$$$ to $$$(x, y)$$$, or tell him that it's impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer number $$$n~(1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5)$$$ — the number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains the sequence of operations — a string of $$$n$$$ characters. Each character is either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains two integers $$$x, y~(-10^9 \\le x, y \\le 10^9)$$$ — the coordinates of the cell where the robot should end its path."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the minimum possible length of subsegment that can be changed so the resulting sequence of operations moves the robot from $$$(0, 0)$$$ to $$$(x, y)$$$. If this change is impossible, print $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\nRURUU\n-2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\nRULR\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\nUUU\n100 100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example the sequence can be changed to "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"U"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"UU"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". So the length of the changed subsegment is $$$3 - 1 + 1 = 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example the given sequence already leads the robot to $$$(x, y)$$$, so the length of the changed subsegment is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example the robot can't end his path in the cell $$$(x, y)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1073C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1073/problem/C"}